I wrote the script for the iMet-XQ2, based on the earlier exisitng script used for previous measurements.
The script uses two main libraries, serial for receiving the output from the sensor,
and csv, for real-time writing into the output file. 
The script writes into the relevant csv file once every second, appending the latest output to the end of the file.
It receives the outputs from the sensor on port 57600.
It resets the buffer so irrelevant backlog doesn't get mixed into the current data.
Added: Data normalization for temperature and timezone fix for time.